  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let the area enclosed by the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis, and the tangent and normal drawn to the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "170",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given curve is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;</p><p>On differentiating both sides, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>y</mi><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now, at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>36</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>48</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mfenced><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msup></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So slope of tangent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</p><p>slope of normal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>i.e. equation of tangent&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p>and equation of normal&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Intersection point of tangent and normal is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The intersection point of tangent and normal with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis respectively will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, area of triangle formed&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo></math>Base<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo></math>Height</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>31</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><mn>85</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>85</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>170</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}